  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Breeding and growing pigs in Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Presently, all pork meat that is sold in the targeted supermarkets in the Inhambane region is imported from South Africa&#xA0;&#x2013; just like many of the meat products sold in Mozambique. In order to become competitive, to increase shelf life and to secure the availability, the companies Blue Magnolia South Africa and Mozambique Organicos Mozambique jointed by a private person will establish a piggery farm in Inhacoongo, Inhambane province, Mozambique.The project includes a breeding facility a growing facility and an abattoir. The capacity of the facility is 2,000 pigs per year which is sufficient to serve the three supermarkets of the guarantor Taurus, Mozambique. The facility, which is considered to be the first commercial modern piggery will be HACCP certified. The facility will apply all modern EU standard technologies. A training centre will be established in cooperation with the Universidade Eduardo Mondlane to assist local farms in piggery. Feedstock for the piggery will be sourced locally as much as possible.</narrative>
  </description>
